          "contextHash": "dbc468a14b601d5d9240aeb72b9fcd2f8aed2f4e30932876edf8d16ec313846b"
        },
        {
          "id": "u_991a272209435ca11df5c492_0",
          "kind": "p",
          "source": "Naming software is hard. I lived in Ontario when I first started the project and Trillium (the flower) is sort of a provincial logo, many institutions in Ontario are named \"Trillium [something]\". So I kept hearing/reading it almost everyday, I liked the sound of it and its nature motif, so I just reused it.",
          "sourceHash": "991a272209435ca11df5c4923fe5f6bd47bfc0b10bccf7513d855c01aa7a0e87",
          "context": "FAQ > Inspiration for the name “Trilium”",
          "contextHash": "2aefba86ecae4c45e8cbdeeced1f92fbc3bfb03a8025f12299fe8284a7d41b73"
        },
        {
          "id": "u_272aaae04764feaaa140f592_0",
          "kind": "p",
          "source": "__TRILIUM_PH_0__– Zadam (original Trilium maintainer)__TRILIUM_PH_1__",
          "sourceHash": "272aaae04764feaaa140f592e8bae164f3fae61a655492ee3a5fc0b99e446dec",
          "context": "FAQ > Inspiration for the name “Trilium”",
          "contextHash": "2aefba86ecae4c45e8cbdeeced1f92fbc3bfb03a8025f12299fe8284a7d41b73"
        },
        {
          "id": "u_f905b755b57f5274f6144536_0",
          "kind": "p",
          "source": "Despite the fact that the Trillium flower has two “l\"s, the Trilium application only has one.",
          "sourceHash": "f905b755b57f5274f6144536b62319ffdd23bfa943df617dbeceb263e76c3ce6",
          "context": "FAQ > Inspiration for the name “Trilium”",
          "contextHash": "2aefba86ecae4c45e8cbdeeced1f92fbc3bfb03a8025f12299fe8284a7d41b73"
        },
        {
          "id": "u_8ed75cb77c507e3e017e7d90_0",
          "kind": "p",
          "source": "Trilium has no separate folder type: any note can have child notes, so any note can act as a folder. A note can hold its own content and have children at the same time, unlike a file system, which separates files from directories.",
          "sourceHash": "8ed75cb77c507e3e017e7d9003996c6e2c9d54a306b48a7ffba1483f00ab7a99",
          "context": "FAQ > How do I create a folder?",
          "contextHash": "1e0c9dd2ddb46e877164a8a61a051b1c31039b151eb80fbbd0db25e9503d5100"
        },
        {
          "id": "u_4f15f782c15b8530aa4e9aac_0",
          "kind": "p",
          "source": "To organize notes into a folder:",
          "sourceHash": "4f15f782c15b8530aa4e9aac4a2330c12a3e6bf6f0fba36b9fd08ac8c04025f1",
          "context": "FAQ > How do I create a folder?",
          "contextHash": "1e0c9dd2ddb46e877164a8a61a051b1c31039b151eb80fbbd0db25e9503d5100"
        },
        {
          "id": "u_eb401a1e73a96ec6e920bda4_0",
          "kind": "li",
          "source": "Create a note that acts as the folder, for example \"Projects\".",
          "sourceHash": "eb401a1e73a96ec6e920bda405c74c8adad1cd975568b8328a80a195dd491b96",
          "context": "FAQ > How do I create a folder?",
          "contextHash": "1e0c9dd2ddb46e877164a8a61a051b1c31039b151eb80fbbd0db25e9503d5100"
        }
      ]
    }
